{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' /app/agent-output/S22-duplicate-insert-boot-crash-trap/report.md && echo '--- fixture status ---' && find /app/fixture -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f %s bytes\\\\n' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"# S22 — Duplicate insert boot-crash report\n\n## 1. Root cause\n\nThe collision is between these two declarations of the same loader-entry ID:\n\n- The profile’s manually added block in `profile-patch-excerpt.txt`:\n  `id: workspace-files`, `name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-workspace-files'`.\n- The installed web-app bundle’s block in `web-app-patch-excerpt.txt`:\n  `id: workspace-files`, `name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-workspace-files'` (identified as L110–111 in the installed tree).\n\nThe duplicate is detected at the Cordis loader layer, specifically in\n`cordis-plugin-loader`’s `EntryGroup.update`, while `dsh-app-boot` applies the\n`cordis:include` loader entry. It is not a failure in the workspace-files\nplugin’s runtime or document-reading code.\n\nLoader-entry IDs are unique keys in the merged include/entry group. An `insert`\nis a declaration/addition, not a later-row override, so accepting the second\nrow would make the composed loader tree ambiguous (including which declaration\nand metadata should win). Cordis therefore throws on the duplicate and aborts\nplugin-tree construction; no web boot can continue.\n\n## 2. Layering rules\n\nFor a profile patch over a bundle-provided plugin:\n\n- Changing that plugin’s configuration by its existing ID is safe; it targets\n  the existing declaration rather than declaring a second one.\n- Inserting an ID that the bundle does not ship is safe as an additional\n  profile/plugin declaration.\n- Inserting an ID that the bundle already ships is fatal because it creates a\n  duplicate loader entry.\n\nThe maintainer performed the third operation. The proof is the matching\n`workspace-files` row in the web-app bundle excerpt, alongside the identical\nmanual row in the profile excerpt. The profile comment calling the row\n“冗余” is therefore correct about its redundancy, but retaining the row is not\nsafe: redundancy in an `insert` is precisely the duplicate.\n\n## 3. Fix\n\nDelete the manually added `workspace-files` `- insert:` block from the profile’s\n`cordis.patch.yml` (the block at the end of `profile-patch-excerpt.txt`). Keep\nthe bundle’s existing row. If the profile needs to adjust this plugin, change\nits configuration by the existing ID instead of inserting another loader row.\n\nThe plugin’s own code is not at fault. The loader fails while composing the\nplugin tree, before the plugin can be initialized, so no plugin-side code\nchange can resolve this boot failure. The required change is in the profile\npatch; changing or removing the bundle plugin itself would be the wrong fix.\n\n## 4. Prevention\n\nBefore adding a loader row by hand, inspect the installed bundle’s\n`cordis.patch.yml` (and the installed package/tree it references) for the\nplugin ID. In this incident, checking the web-app bundle would have shown the\n`workspace-files` row already supplied at L110–111.\n\nAt boot, dsh could make the diagnostic actionable by reporting both declaration\nowners and their sources, for example: profile\n`C:\\Users\\lhh\\.dsh\\profiles\\web\\cordis.patch.yml` and the web-app bundle’s\n`packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml`, then explicitly advising:\n\n> Duplicate loader entry `workspace-files`: bundle already provides\n> `@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-workspace-files`; remove the profile’s manual `insert`\n> block from the profile patch.\n\nThat identifies whom to blame (the profile-side duplicate), what is already\nprovided (the bundle), and exactly what to delete.\n--- fixture status ---\nREADME.md 614 bytes\nboot-crash-log.txt 1544 bytes\nprofile-patch-excerpt.txt 767 bytes\nweb-app-patch-excerpt.txt 672 bytes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
